WEBVTT

00:00:01.500 --> 00:00:06.180
Recently, researchers have discovered a new bacterium that feeds on plastics.
最近，研究人员发现了一种以塑料为食的新细菌。

00:00:06.980 --> 00:00:14.020
Scientists say the discovery could help reduce a flood of plastics that are ending up in the landfills and polluting oceans.
科学家说，大量塑料正源源不断地流入垃圾填埋场、污染海洋，而这一发现可能有助于减少这些塑料。

00:00:14.820 --> 00:00:18.930
Plastic is one of the most difficult materials to break down or recycle.
塑料是最难分解或回收的材料之一。

00:00:19.730 --> 00:00:26.730
To solve the problem, a team from the Helmholtz Center for Environmental Research in Germany found the new soil bacterium.
为了解决这个问题，德国亥姆霍兹环境研究中心的一个团队找到了这种新的土壤细菌。

00:00:27.530 --> 00:00:30.390
It was found in an area with a lot of plastic wastes.
它是在一个有大量塑料垃圾的地方发现的。

00:00:31.190 --> 00:00:37.740
The team discovered the bacterium could feed on polyurethane, which is widely used in making different plastic products.
该团队发现，这种细菌能以聚氨酯为食，而聚氨酯广泛用于制造各种塑料制品。

00:00:38.540 --> 00:00:44.310
It was reported that polyurethane made up 3.5 million tons of Europe’s plastics last year.
据报道，去年欧洲的塑料中，聚氨酯占了350万吨。

00:00:45.110 --> 00:00:49.360
One problem is that recycling polyurethane requires a lot of energy.
问题之一是，回收聚氨酯需要耗费大量能源。

00:00:50.160 --> 00:00:55.740
So most polyurethane-based wastes are sent to landfills, where they can give off dangerous chemicals.
所以，大多数聚氨酯类垃圾被送往垃圾填埋场，并可能在那里释放出危险的化学物质。

00:00:56.540 --> 00:01:01.050
The team found that the bacterium could produce enzymes that could eat polyurethane.
该团队发现，这种细菌能产生可以吃掉聚氨酯的酶。

00:01:01.850 --> 00:01:04.750
This would make it possible to break down plastic wastes.
这将使分解塑料垃圾成为可能。

00:01:05.550 --> 00:01:08.840
The results were recently reported in a science magazine.
这些研究结果最近发表在一本科学杂志上。

00:01:09.640 --> 00:01:11.780
Hermann Heipieper helped write the report.
赫尔曼·海皮佩尔协助撰写了这份报告。

00:01:12.580 --> 00:01:18.030
He said that the finding “marks an important step in being able to reuse hard-to-recycle products”.
他说，这一发现“标志着在实现难以回收产品的再利用方面迈出了重要一步”。

00:01:18.830 --> 00:01:24.150
The research is part of a European Union program that tries to find useful bacteria.
这项研究是欧盟一个项目的一部分，这个项目设法寻找有用的细菌。

00:01:24.950 --> 00:01:31.750
The goal is to discover living things that can help turn plastics into materials that can be broken down biologically.
其目标是发现一些生物，它们能帮助把塑料变成可以通过生物方式分解的材料。

00:01:32.550 --> 00:01:39.180
Some scientists advise against introducing the bacteria into the environment at present, which could be harmful.
一些科学家建议目前不要把这种细菌引入环境，这样做可能有害。

00:01:39.980 --> 00:01:44.990
It is suggested that much more study should be carried out to learn more about the bacterium.
有人建议，应该再开展大量研究，进一步了解这种细菌。

00:01:45.790 --> 00:01:53.230
“Such research is needed before we can take action such as putting the plastic-eating bacteria into the oceans,” a scientist said.
一位科学家说：“需要先开展这样的研究，然后我们才能采取行动，比如把这种吃塑料的细菌投放到海洋中。”
